4	\label{sec:perf_metrics}
5	
6	The following sections present performance, power, and architecture metrics for
7	different build configurations and AIE graph architectures. All configurations
8	are derived from the same stepped-frequency X-band radar dataset. The waveform
9	and frequency parameters are therefore fixed across all tests and are
10	summarized in Table~\ref{tab:global_radar_params}. These constants define the
11	underlying radar physics, while configuration-specific parameters (e.g., number
12	of pulses, range-compressed samples, and aperture size) vary per experiment and
13	are reported in the subsequent subsections.
14	
15	\begin{table}[hbt]
16	  \centering
17	  \caption{Global radar characteristics (constant for all configurations).}
18	  \label{tab:global_radar_params}
19	  \begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
20	    \toprule
21	    \textbf{Parameter} & \textbf{Value} \\
22	    \midrule
23	    Physical frequency samples ($N_f$) & 424 \\
24	    Frequency step ($\Delta f$) & 1.4713026 MHz \\
25	    Start frequency ($f_{\min}$) & 9.2880804 GHz \\
26	    Stop frequency ($f_{\max}$)  & 9.9119127 GHz \\
27	    Center frequency ($f_0$)     & 9.5999966 GHz \\
28	    Wavelength ($\lambda = c/f_0$) & 3.12 cm \\
29	    Polarization & HH \\
30	    Dataset source & GOTCHA (pass 1) \\
31	    \bottomrule
32	  \end{tabular}
33	\end{table}
34	
35	All timing measurements are captured using \texttt{CLOCK\_MONOTONIC} on the ARM
36	Cortex-A72 processor. Estimated power consumption was derived using the
37	\gls{xpe} tool and actual power draw was captured from INA226 current-sense
38	monitors on the VCK190 board.
